<title>INDIA: India IDBI 1996/97 1st half net up 2 pct.</title>
<headline>India IDBI 1996/97 1st half net up 2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		5,140.0 vs  5,030.0</p>
<p>    Operating income     27,760.0 vs 23,570.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	    21,230.0 vs 17,270.0</p>
<p>    Interest		 19,770.0 vs 16,270.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation		670.0 vs    350.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	6,530.0 vs  6,300.0</p>
<p>    Capital gains	     240.0 vs    230.0</p>
<p>    Profit before tax     6,770.0 vs  6,530.0</p>
<p>    Taxation		  1,640.0 vs  1,500.0</p>
<p>    Sanctions		83,420.0 vs108,360.0</p>
<p>    Disbursals	     59,690.0 vs 51,120.0</p>
<p>    Share (in rupees)     15.02   vs   15.07</p>
<p>Note: The Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI) is India's largest term-lending financial institution. The results are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
